as an example because that's not what I was saying at all, you know, it's really it's his job to make sure that the props are right and this our job to make sure that the props are right and there's our job to make sure that the props are right And this is just the kind of back and forth the everyday back and forth that we go through when we're making things for a film set So when you're doing that script breakdown What are some of the key words that you're looking for that indicate that you have work to do in that scene? The word that always stops me in my tracks when I'm reading a script would be the word office Because offices are just absolutely full of paperwork. You know, like notice boards and filing cabinets and desks covered in all kinds of paperwork.
作为例子了，因为那根本不是我想表达的意思，你知道，确保道具正确本来就是他的工作，确保道具正确也是我们的工作，确保道具正确也是我们的工作。这就是我们在为电影布景制作东西时所经历的那种来回沟通，日常的来回沟通。所以在做剧本拆解时，你在寻找哪些关键词来表明你在那个场景中有工作要做呢？每当我读剧本时，总有一个词能让我停下脚步，那就是“办公室”。因为办公室里绝对塞满了各种纸质文件。你知道，比如公告栏、文件柜以及堆满各种纸质文件的办公桌。

