14
00:07:36.000 --> 00:08:12.000
that looking things up on the internet can be misleading for a couple of reasons. First of all, nobody really ever labels anything properly online. Like if you find, if you find a beautiful vintage map on Tumblr, there's absolutely no way it's going to tell you what year it's from or what the dimensions of it are. And then also, it's really difficult to judge by looking at pictures on a screen, the scale of things, and also the texture of things. So if I have to make a telegram, for example, I really need to go to a flea market and find an old telegram that I can hold in my hands,
在网上查阅资料可能会由于几个原因而产生误导。首先，网上的东西从来没有人真正好好归类过。比如如果你在Tumblr上找到一张精美的复古地图，绝对没有办法告诉你它是哪一年的或者它的尺寸是多少。其次，通过看屏幕上的图片，真的很难判断事物的比例以及质感。所以如果我必须制作一份电报，例如，我真的需要去跳蚤市场找到一份可以拿在手里的旧电报，

